<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Morro do Castelo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Morro do Castelo was a hill in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> to which the young city was moved in 1567 under Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mem-de-sa">Mem de Sá</a>, after the French were driven out. It held the first fort, cathedral and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> college of the city. The hill was levelled in 1920–1922 to make room for modern development.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/morro-do-castelo.jpg" alt="Morro do Castelo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nikolof · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pal%C3%A1cio_Tiradentes_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
